# WaterSourceSpecs

 + Grauschweif.WaterSourceSpecs.ImmutableWaterSourceSpec -> ignores modifiers and keeps initial strength
 + Grauschweif.WaterSourceSpecs.CleanWaterSourceSpec -> ignores badtide modifier and keeps initial strength
 +  Grauschweif.WaterSourceSpecs.DroughtResistingWaterSourceSpec -> halves drought effect

# WhitepawsPatchSpec

```
{
  'WhitepawsPatchSpec': {
    'FactionId': 'Whitepaws', // single faction only, or 'Common' (faction > common)
    'SwimmingPenalty': -1.0,  // -1 would double swim speed; game default is 0.3 or 30% slowdown
    'WaterUnitsPerVoxel': 8,  // amount of water extracted per voxel; default is 5, so 60% more here
    'HideNeedApplicationProbability': true
    //    'HideNeedApplicationProbabilityLocKey': 'EffectProbability.Hidden', 
    }
}
```

# NeedEffectDescriber patch

The colours of chance effects in workspaces etc. now reflect if the change is positive or negative (i.e. points are given or taken for need).
Vanilla decorator only based it on need having possible positive value and ignored the effect completely!

Might extend that to other describers (likely json-configurable) if needed. For example a building that had range / continuous effect of injury, thirst etc, would display that in green ▲ - same if it healed instead. it's always only green..
